{
  "_": [
    "The shot list for nus.dev. scripts/shots.ps1 launches the app once per shot,",
    "per face (paper, ink), drives it with these steps, and captures the window.",
    "",
    "Each shot: name, what it is for on the site, an optional `type` (NUS_TYPE:",
    "typed into the first shell at its first prompt, \\n = Enter), `settle` ms to",
    "wait after the window shows, then `steps`. A step is one of:",
    "  { \"key\": \"ctrl+shift+k\" }       a chord, by physical key",
    "  { \"type\": \"cargo te\" }           text, as typed (Unicode input)",
    "  { \"wait\": 800 }                    milliseconds",
    "  { \"click\": [x, y] }               logical px from the window's top-left",
    "  { \"altclick\": [x, y] }            Alt held",
    "  { \"hover\": [x, y] }",
    "`crop` is a fraction of the window [x, y, w, h]; without it the whole window",
    "is saved. `relaunch: true` starts the app a second time before capturing,",
    "so the first run leaves a session behind (the atlas needs one).",
    "A page in the split is opened through the url palette (ctrl+shift+l), not NUS_TYPE:",
    "NUS_TYPE writes to the PTY, and the URL rule is the app's, not the shell's.",
    "`todo` marks a shot the harness cannot drive yet; it is skipped and listed."
  ],
  "window": {
    "logical": [
      1280,
      800
    ]
  },
  "shell": "pwsh",
  "url": "http://localhost:8000/",
  "shots": [
